-- 1007: Injection and structural foam calculators, version 2 -- plasticizing and ejection in the cycle; holding pressure no longer counted twice.
--
-- GENERATED by scripts/generate-plastic-molding-calculators-migration.ts from
-- src/modules/bom-items/costing/plastic-molding/calculators/plastic-molding-calculators.json.
-- Do not edit by hand: change the spec and regenerate.
--
-- ROOT CAUSE
--
-- The injection cycle (migration 975) was fill + pack + cooling + mold open/close. The Menges cooling time runs from the end of filling to ejection, and
-- holding pressure acts inside that time, so the separate pack phase (35 % of cooling, at least 2 s) counted it twice. The reference states the inputs of
-- the phases the cycle left out, read by nothing: the press plasticizing rate (or plasticizingRateByClampForce) with plasticizingRateMultiplier, the
-- ejector variables (ejectorDistanceFactor, ejectorPercentMaxMachineVelocity, numEjectorCycles, dryCycleStrokeFactor) and injectionRateMultiplier.
-- Version 2: cycle = injection + cooling + the plasticizing that outlasts cooling + ejection (mold open/close + the ejector stroke), each a calculator
-- field shown on the line (formula registry F-05 v2, F-08 v2, F-20, F-21). The calculators are replaced under version 2; LSR, compression and RIM are
-- unchanged.
--
-- This migration creates one global calculator per spec entry (inputs are the
-- values the cost engine seeds, each shown with its source in the calculation
-- trace; calculated fields are the formulas the engine evaluates, it holds
-- none) and links every Plastic Molding catalog operation it computes to its
-- calculator in process_calculator_mappings.
--
-- Requires migration 804 (calculators.retired_at).
-- Self-contained, idempotent, post-checked.

BEGIN;

-- Injection Molding - Cycle Time
DO $calc$
DECLARE v_id UUID;
